          "text": "## Position-aware capability decision (v0.0.21)\n\nRoute matched exactly: `position-aware-capability-negative` (\"async func(u64) -> map<string,u64> as an ordinary public WAsmC value\"). Its `required_additional_reads` is empty and it names no check command, so no further artifacts are needed.\n\n**Whole-request decision:** unsupported as a whole. `u64` is supported by the v0.0.21 compiler, but async ordinary source and a direct public map result are *independently* unsupported. Positions must be decided separately:\n\n### 1. Source position — ordinary synchronous function with a `u64` parameter\n**Supported.** The v0.0.21 compiler accepts ordinary source with a `u64` parameter, and `u64` preserves width and signedness. Supported ordinary-source `u64` positions:\n- `u64` ordinary local\n- `u64` parameter\n- `u64` result\n- `u64` nested source payload\n\nSo an ordinary synchronous function accepting `u64` can be compiled.\n\n### 2. Public-value position — `map<string,u64>` as a direct public value result\n**Unsupported.** A resident/local Map is not a direct public WIT value result; Map is resident/local only.\n\n### 3. Async position — publicly exposed async function\n**Unsupported.** Ordinary async source remains unsupported in v0.0.21. This is an independent stop from the Map/`u64` issue.\n\n### 4. Host position — separate authority\n**Separate from compilation and not granted.** A declared import is an effect request; it grants no filesystem, network, clock, randomness, process, credential or device authority, and installation grants no Host authority. Host use requires inspecting every generated import before instantiation and comparing module, name, kind and signature against an application-owned exact allowlist; pure programs require `imports=[]` and instantiate with `{}`.\n\n## Semantics-preserving alternatives (unsupported positions only)\nPer the route, alternatives only for the unsupported positions, and **no source is generated**:\n- `u32` or `i64` only with application-owned bounds and signedness proof\n- ordered `list<Entry<K,V>>` snapshot only when copied-value semantics are equivalent\n- declared resource for identity and mutation\n- otherwise stop\n\nPosition summary: source `u64` = supported; public `map<string,u64>` = unsupported; async = unsupported; Host = separate authority, not implied by any of the above."
        },
